  "question": {
    "text": "Two magnetic dipoles <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> are placed at a separation <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> , with their axes perpendicular to each other. The dipole moment of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> is twice that of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> . A particle of charge <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></math> is passing through their mid-point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> , at angle <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> with the horizontal line, as shown in figure. What would be the magnitude of force on the particle at that instant? ( <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> is much larger than the dimension of the dipole)<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0191_ac27511d9050.png\" />"
