  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> along <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> -axis<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mtext>Y</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math> along <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math> -axis<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mtext>X</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></msub></math></p><p>Hence <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub></math> will be at <math><msup><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> from <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> -axis.<br />Now, velocity and magnetic field are in same direction. Hence no force will act on the particle.</p>"
